ecting to feel so much  like a normal band  but having the elasticity am i saying  that right less to see  let's go ahead and swap this out since i  was really looking forward to this new  braided solo loop and i think this one  is gonna be very popular so it's great  that you can still get it with the se  before i compare the exteriors let's do  a quick test and  no it's too loose oh my goodness  um now man i checked the sizing using  apple's little print out  and it seemed like i ordered the right  one let's do a double check here  yeah the right in between eight or nine  for me if you guys could see that  i went with the nine and i wish i didn't  now i'm gonna have to return this and i  really don't want to  but i can't deal with it flopping around  so that definitely is a disappointment  so  go on the smaller side absolutely don't  if you're closer to one just take one  step down because this probably is going  to stretch  after a while just like other people are  saying now let's compare the exteriors  and obviously this one's smaller but  other than that they're identical if we  look at the left side  the speakers the little ports look  identical the right side the button the  microphone cut out  the crown looks identical my se does  have lte  because i want to set it up for my kid  my series six doesn't so that's why you  don't see that little line  but other than that they're the same now  let's compare the sensors  i have my watch band off let's flip  these and compare the sensors and we  definitely see  a difference so it looks like the se has  the design from the series  5 and the series 6 has a whole new  design we have  uh four led lights four sensors in the  center because it could do  blood oxygen sensing so that the se  can not do but the se also looks  different let me grab my other apple  watches  it's crazy i have five apple watches  here that's weird but let's start out  with  the series five and it's interesting to  see  that the centers are the same here but  the outside is different  just like on that series six we have  these two outside portions  a ring around it my series 5 also has it  but the se does not have that so that  has to be  for the ecg feature which the se  doesn't have let's add in the series 3  there's a huge difference here the  casing is much larger with just a little  central circle  and then we have some lights two lights  and then looks like two sensors  so it's definitely an upgrade from that  so now we know that the se  is just like the series four and the  series 5  just without the ecg now i also have my  series  0 original apple watch it's interesting  to see that the sensors are the same as  the series 3.  if you guys want to see a full  comparison between the se and the series  3 what you get for the  extra eighty dollars go ahead and click  that little subscribe button down below  enable those notifications  now let's get into the displays and  thankfully the se  is using the same display as the siri  six  that means if you're using a full screen  watch face  or if you have photos that are showing  up you get these nice  rounded corners and the screen size is  larger with slimmer bezels  than you would on a series 3 or an older  apple watch so that is great now the  display tech  is also the same it's using a ltpo  display  so that uses less power but with the se  you don't have the ability to have an  always on display so that's something  that apple  locks out just with software to you know  make a little bit of a difference there  so as you guys see with this watch face  we still have the always on the sc you  don't so you have to raise up your wrist  and then you see it just like with a lot  of the older apple watches  on a positive note you do still get all  of the same watch faces so here's the  typography watch face  so you're not limited in that along with  sharing the watch faces they  also share a ton of other features i  have a full list right here  they both have the same file detection  the same second generation heart rate  sensors  the same accelerometers they have uh the  same  speaker the same microphone the same 32  gigabytes of storage which i was  surprised by  the same w3 chip and the same bluetooth  5  and the series 5 actually shares that as  well  so it's kind of like a series 5 but  there's one thing that the se  gets from the series 6 that the 5  doesn't have and that's the always on  altimeter that means that the se along  with the six they can always tell  your altitude which is great if you're a  hiker that gives  more information for your workouts so  your watch will know  when you're going up in elevation they  can apply that to the calories you burn  and other aspects  which could be nice if you do a lot of  hiking so with so many of the same  features and specs what does the series  6  give you well the first one is the  ability to do ecgs  which will check your heart for  irregular heartbeats  the next one is blood oxygen sensing so  if you're somebody that could have some  health issues  or like my son he has asthma and  allergies  that could be really handy the seri six  has the new u1 chip that is included  with the new iphones  now one thing we know is it's gonna make  it a lot easier to find your watch if  you left it somewhere  but there's probably gonna be a lot more  features that go along with that that  we'll find out at next month's apple  event  the six is the first watch that can  connect to five gigahertz wi-fi  so it could give you some better range  and also some faster transfer speeds  for say you know music photos things  like that but i haven't really noticed  an issue  with mine and then along with that it  also has the s6  processor which is about 20 uh faster  let's do a quick test here see if we can  notice a difference  so as far as switching between watch  faces both are super smooth  let's go to our home page i have it set  up a little bit differently  but uh based on what i've been playing  around right now with the se  it seems plenty fast has the same  processor as the series 5 which is  already  a very fast processor now i will say  with my series 5  i did occasionally notice some glitches  sometimes when i'd go in to  adjust the watch you'd get a little  glitch in the animation that could be  once you're using the watch for a while  you have a bunch of apps on it you have  stuff running in the background  but it is not bad with the siri six i've  been using it over the weekend and it is  definitely a little bit smoother  so with all of that said let's get into  prices and then talk about  which one you should buy the base  starting price of the series 6  is 3.99 or 400 and the se is 279 so  that's a 120  difference and that is pretty  significant  now i did say at the start that the  prices get a little bit more  interesting it's a bigger difference  than you'd expect and that is because if  you're  buying one with lte the series six and  all the previous apple watches  apple would charge an extra 100 dollars  for that lte option so it was a pricey  upgrade  surprisingly and thankfully with the se  apple is only charging 50 more if you  want lte  so that brings the price difference to  170  dollars that is very significant and  you'll need the lte if you want to set  up  one for say your kid or a family member  you have to have the lte set up so with  that price difference being  so big you can actually buy an se you  can add on lte  even if you might not use it right away  you can upgrade to a different watch  band like the new solo braided loop  and you're still twenty dollars cheaper  than the very base model  basic apple watch series six so that is  a very impressive difference and gives  you a lot of value with the se  so with the ses value being so good  why would you spend the extra money on  the series six well there's just a few  reasons the first ones are if you have  health issues or if there's health  issues  in the family you want to have that ecg  ability  you want to have the blood oxygen  sensors that's going to be a no-brainer  to spend the extra money  and along with that if you want the  extra finishes say if you want to get a  stainless steel one  or you want to get the red or the blue  you have to get the series six apple is  locking that just for the higher end  models and then another one that's going  to be a big one for a lot of people is  the always on display  having the ability to see the time see  notifications and just have a little bit  of a nicer look  when the screen is off instead of having  it be purely black  that is going to be another big reason  but with that said i think for the vast  majority of people  the se just makes a ton of sense apple's  packing in a lot of value  it's almost like a series five that cost  way more last year  so let us know your thoughts and which  one you want to go with down in the  comment section below we're gonna have  links to both in the video description  a lot of times there's great deals on  amazon so make sure to go and check  those out  and if you want to see our full review  after we use these click that circle  above to subscribe  and if you want to set it up for your  kid we have a video for you as well  thank you for watching it's been max and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]

